# ============================================================================
# Append to /etc/hosts on EVERY node (needs sudo).
# ============================================================================
#
# WHY, when the mesh already provides DNS: on at least one of our five machines
# the mesh's own DNS was not reachable from inside WSL2 - /etc/resolv.conf held
# only the WSL NAT resolver, so mesh names did not resolve at all. A static
# block costs nothing and removes DNS from the list of things that can break the
# cluster at 2am.
#
# See wsl.conf in this directory: WSL rewrites /etc/hosts on every boot unless
# you tell it not to, which will silently undo this file.

100.64.0.10   master
100.64.0.11   worker1
100.64.0.12   worker2
100.64.0.13   worker3
100.64.0.14   worker4
